---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon — Ed Chapman"
  description="How edwardchapman.co.uk is built: Astro on Cloudflare Workers, static-first, spec-driven, with its architecture decisions public."
>
  <h1>Colophon</h1>
  <p>
    How this site is built — because for a personal site by an engineer, the
    <em>how</em> is part of the point. A fuller version of this page ships with the
    site's first full release; the source is already public.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Static by design.</strong> Built with Astro, served from Cloudflare
      Workers Static Assets. There is no origin server — the previous incarnation
      of this domain died with one; this one structurally cannot.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Spec-first.</strong> The commissioning specification and every load-bearing
      architecture decision are in the repository as ADRs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Gated.</strong> Every change lands through a PR that must pass a single
      deterministic gate — format, lint, types, tests, build, a content-safety scan,
      and built-output link checks.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The full details live in the
    <a href={SITE.repo}>public repository</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
